            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous coronary artery dissection associated with sexual intercourse.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1323-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of spontaneous coronary artery dissection associated with sexual intercourse in a 32-year-old, morbidly obese patient. This is the first report of spontaneous coronary artery dissection induced by coital activity and the sixth such report in a male patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
